WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.260
Every one of my apps signs
in through one server.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.325
If that server is wrong,
every app is wrong.

3
00:00:07.825 --> 00:00:10.254
A sign-in server set up by hand drifts.

4
00:00:10.554 --> 00:00:15.455
And an upgrade can quietly bring back
a default sign-in flow, a second,

5
00:00:15.455 --> 00:00:16.422
weaker way in.

6
00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:19.059
So nothing here is set up by hand.

7
00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:24.038
One file, over fifteen hundred lines
long, describes the whole server.

8
00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:26.863
But a file only says what should be true.

9
00:00:27.163 --> 00:00:32.990
So after every deploy, a check runs inside
the server, against the live database.

10
00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.400
It tests thirty-seven promises.

11
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.998
Only my own sign-in flows exist.

12
00:00:38.198 --> 00:00:41.407
Every app sends people back
to an exact secure address.

13
00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.691
No app is open to every account.

14
00:00:43.891 --> 00:00:45.965
There is exactly one administrator.

15
00:00:46.465 --> 00:00:50.347
When all thirty-seven hold,
it prints invariants OK.

16
00:00:50.847 --> 00:00:53.059
Now slip one default flow back in.

17
00:00:53.359 --> 00:00:56.371
One lock stays open, and the deploy fails.
